      "explanation": [
        "Main idea: bringen means to bring, take or deliver: to get something or someone to a particular place. Irregular forms: bringt, brachte, hat gebracht. It often has two objects: jemandem (Dat) etwas (Akk) bringen.",
        "In a figurative sense it means to achieve a result: Das bringt nichts (that is no use), Das bringt mich auf eine Idee. With zu + noun it forms fixed expressions.",
        "Unlike holen, which means to go and fetch, bringen only expresses delivering something."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Kannst du mir bitte ein Glas Wasser bringen?",
          "lv": "Could you bring me a glass of water, please?"
        },
        {
          "de": "Ich bringe die Kinder zur Schule.",
          "lv": "I take the children to school."
        },
        {
          "de": "Der Kellner bringt die Rechnung.",
          "lv": "The waiter brings the bill."
        },
        {
          "de": "Sie bringt ihre Tochter nach Hause.",
          "lv": "She takes her daughter home."
        },
        {
          "de": "Der Brief bringt gute Nachrichten.",
          "lv": "The letter brings good news."
        }
      ],
      "comparison": [
        {
          "word": "holen",
          "meaning": "to fetch",
          "example": "Ich hole die Kinder. – I'll fetch the children."
        },
        {
          "word": "mitbringen",
          "meaning": "to bring along",
          "example": "Ich bringe Kuchen mit. – I'm bringing a cake with me."
        },
        {
          "word": "tragen",
          "meaning": "to carry",
          "example": "Er trägt die Tasche. – He is carrying the bag."
        }
      ],
      "tip": [
        "Remember the irregular past: bringen – brachte – gebracht.",
        "Bring somebody something with bringen: Ich bringe dir ein Buch."
      ],
      "important": [
        "The perfect is gebracht, not “gebringt”.",
        "Bringen is not the same as nehmen: nehmen means to take hold of something, bringen means to carry it to a place."
      ],
