      "layout": "standardStudy",
      "translation": "Fire",
      "explanation": [
        "Main idea: das Feuer is a neuter noun; the plural is die Feuer. It means fire (a campfire, a fire in the fireplace) and also a blaze: Im Haus ist Feuer ausgebrochen.",
        "Common expressions: Feuer machen (to light a fire), Feuer! (the cry for a fire), Hast du Feuer? (have you got a light?). The fire brigade is die Feuerwehr."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Wir machen ein Feuer am See.",
          "lv": "We are lighting a fire by the lake."
        },
        {
          "de": "Das Feuer brennt im Kamin.",
          "lv": "The fire is burning in the fireplace."
        },
        {
          "de": "Im Haus ist Feuer ausgebrochen.",
          "lv": "A fire broke out in the house."
        },
        {
          "de": "Hast du Feuer?",
          "lv": "Have you got a light?"
        }
      ],
      "comparison": [
        {
          "word": "der Brand",
          "meaning": "fire, blaze (more formal)",
          "example": "Der Brand zerstörte das Haus. – The fire destroyed the house."
        },
        {
          "word": "die Flamme",
          "meaning": "flame",
          "example": "Die Flamme ist klein. – The flame is small."
        },
        {
          "word": "die Feuerwehr",
          "meaning": "fire brigade",
          "example": "Die Feuerwehr kommt sofort. – The fire brigade is coming at once."
        }
      ],
      "tip": [
        "A destructive fire is more formally der Brand; Feuer is broader and also covers a fire that has been lit."
      ],
      "important": [
        "Do not confuse das Feuer (fire) with die Feuerwehr (fire brigade)."
      ],
